// expect-exit: 0
mod:redef_reroot_store_ok;
// 2026-11-16 (landing 177d2b9, row 4, the tests row: no source change; it pins rows 1-3, the stack, by verdicts). Row 2 (DEF-685's D5) marks a
// pointer parameter its callee re-points (`pp = p2`; also through its own slot, the call road or a branch) and reads that parameter's chain by
// the marked key. Row 3 (DEF-644 root B, S4) reroots an address taken through another pointer (`r = @(<-q0)` over `q0 = @pp`; `@((<-pp).q)`) to
// that pointer's targets, and `rrti_path`'s and `rrti_chain`'s descents read the rerooted targets' chains by row 2's marked key. So a store
// through such an address in a callee is recorded on what the caller passed only when both rows are in: the stack records what no single row
// records. A fix only adds records beside main's.
// THE CONTROLS AND RIGHT PROGRAMS (31), each running 67 on main (acb78ea), on every single row and here: the controls of the faces in
// redef_reroot_store_faces.npk (23), each its face less its growth (`discard(raw growh(hq));`), and the twins of the DEF-690 prices in
// redef_reroot_store_prices.npk (8; 6 since 177d2c): `x_m1a0s1_p2`, `x_m2a0s1_p2`, `x_mba0s1_p2`, `sk_s2p_n2_ok`, `sk_s2p_bn_ok`, `sk_p690_brn_ok`.
// 177d2c row 2 moved `x_m1a0s5_p2` and `x_m1a0s3_p2` there (below). 2026-11-18 (landing 177d2c, row 2 as F-c: rulings l.17976, l.18021 and
// l.18074). Row 2 walks a pointer parameter's own slot THROUGH at a call's first targets, where main cut it, since the callee may write below it; a
// store made by name keeps main's cut. Moved to redef_reroot_store_prices.npk (2), prices at parity: `x_m1a0s5_p2` (l.16636: its store `put2pp(r,
// v)` writes below the slot) and `x_m1a0s3_p2` (l.18074: its callee `setp` writes the slot alone, and F-c reads any call as one that may write
// below it). Added (19): the controls of the faces and pins row 2 adds to redef_reroot_store_faces.npk.
// 2026-11-18 (landing 177d2c, row 3). Added (34): the local twins' controls of the row-3 faces in redef_reroot_store_faces.npk (`b` a local:
// `c3_lc_*` 14, `c4_lc_rr_*` 9, `c5_lc_rr_hd1_ok`, `c5_lc_rr_sl5_ok`, `c6_lc_rr_*` 6) and the three holder twins of `c3_pm_p2_s7_ok`
// (`c3_tw_p2_s7_ok`, `c3_tv_p2_s7_ok`, `c3_tl_p2_s7_ok`), each 67 on main and here.
error:E5;
